Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||03-04-2000||05:21 AM||||My friend's girlfriend's 86GT developed a nasty knock and need a new/different motor. He found a wrecked 86GT and purchased it for $800 and towed it home. We dropped the cradle from the wrecked Fiero then dropped the cradle in the purple Fiero(the girlfriend's). Then the cradle from the wrecked Fiero was installed in the purple Fiero(getting confused yet). Both were 4 speeds. We are getting good at this. <P>For my help I get the fastback clip from the wrecked GT(it was hit in front) and the GT steering wheel and the oilpan. Now I have 2 fastback clips and am going to sell one of them. I am posting it for sale in the Mall section.||||reg||14
Z||000001||wkayl||03-04-2000||03:04 PM||||After I overhauled my son's 84 SE we started with the engine in the cradel sitting behind the car.  4 hrs later we took it for a test drive.  It was easier installing it than removing it.  I think part of that was having never done it on a Fiero before.<P>The oddest swap I ever did was to take a 350 diesel engine out of a '79 Chev pickup and installing an Olds 455 gas in it in 6 hrs.||||reg||1
